{
  "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
  "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Food and Drug Administration",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under the Family Smoking Prevention and Tobacco Control Act, a manufacturer may introduce a new tobacco product only with authorization from the Food and Drug Administration. An applicant must show that the marketing of its product would be appropriate for the protection of the public health, which requires FDA to take into account both the likelihood that existing users of tobacco products will stop using such products and the likelihood that those who do not use tobacco products will start using them if the product is marketed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, in fairness to Respondents, I think their argument is that the guidance were actually a moving target, that either they weren't clear or you changed the -- the guidance as time went on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Food and Drug Administration",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that in this context, the statute gave them the -- the basic calculus that FDA was going to apply. FDA did give guidance saying that this is the way we're thinking about this right now. That was non-binding guidance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you say that it shouldn't apply here because this was the denial of an application, and it was not a punishment. So there's this line of D.C. Circuit cases about airwaves. Could you distinguish those for me? Would we need to worry about those?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wouldn't due process require an opportunity for notice and a hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what was the remedy for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As a practical matter then, I'm curious what relief looks like in this case, because the companies can always reapply, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I wondered if you could tell me why you think that's consistent with -- with Chenery."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus briefs",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0001-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The other side in the amicus briefs sort of say that it was a million --a million plus products that FDA was evaluating at once."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two requirements. One, it helps smoking cessation, and, two, it doesn't create other problems. And two is kind of irrelevant if you fail under one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But wouldn't they still fail under one, that they can't demonstrate a public health benefit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- but it didn't do the work, and so we're going to remand it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm just wondering, does a company ever have a chance to get before a -- a judge and a jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Heyer",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "FDA switched its position on what studies were required and, in so doing, failed to consider applicants' reliance interests in the original instructions and less drastic alternatives. It ignored the marketing plans, and it ignored the notice-and-comment process mandated by the -- the APA and the Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Heyer (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And in your application, you talk about the role of flavors, right, that your application tries to show that if you have flavors, it's better at getting people to quit smoking, right? That's the -- one of the points of your application."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Heyer (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I -- I guess I'm not really seeing what the surprise is here or what the change is here. Like, everybody basically knows that flavors are -- are particularly dangerous in terms of kids starting the use of smoking products."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Heyer (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, this certainly wasn't called out with any -- wasn't called out at all and certainly not with a level of specificity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But isn't it your claim about notice -- I mean, just picking up what -- on -- on what Justice Kagan said, you -- you're claiming: We didn't know we were supposed to be looking at certain things. Am I wrong about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry. I'm so totally confused by your point because the FDA didn't say to you that a longitudinal study was necessary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How -- how is your position consistent with respect to how much guidance has to be provided with the well-recognized authority of agencies to proceed on a case-by-case basis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute says you have to have valid scientific evidence. What -- what if the agency had said you don't have to present any evidence? Is it your position that based on the agency's changing of its position because, at the end of the day, they asked for evidence, that you would be entitled to authorization?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0003-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. So your position is that the switch is clear and that's all we have to decide for you to win?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: The harmless error argument, what do we do about that? Isn't it pretty obvious what will happen on remand if we bother -- require that formality with respect to the marketing plans?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. HEYER",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "given that there is no evidence in the record of what the contents were of the marketing plans that FDA supposedly reviewed and said that these aren't -- and then ignored these -- and, again, it's a post hoc rationalization. FDA didn't even say these aren't any different. It said we're -- we're not looking at them for efficiency purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "scotus-23-1038",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c30ba8c1efdf0d152df794d8e35f4b812e1c7036290d5dea953f42fcb04d813a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c30ba8c1efdf-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF CURTIS E. GANNON ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER MR. GANNON: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. If I could just make three points."
    },
